      <p>As students progress through AT2 and AT3, they take more university courses for credit. The ELI provides students with direct support during this period (e.g. Cohort activities, tutoring, study skills, etc) as well as indirect support, such as training the university instructors to teach international students effectively.</p>
      <p>When students finish AT2, students have enough credits to be considered second semester freshmen. Students who also complete AT3 will earn even more credits. The graphic provides an overview of AT, details about each AT semester are also included in this handbook.</p>
